# Pull in the routing when the card appears.
#
# rotate-audio.service is also wanted by multi-user.target, but the card is not
# necessarily there yet at that point: registration waits on the AGDSP coming
# up and on deferred probe. The unit's ConditionPathExists then skips it - a
# failed condition is never retried - and the routing is never applied at all.
#
# SYSTEMD_WANTS rather than RUN: the unit primes the DSP by spending its first
# (always lost) scene start on silence, which takes a couple of seconds, and a
# RUN program blocks the udev worker for its whole run. systemd's own
# 78-sound-card.rules has already tagged the device by the time this is read.
SUBSYSTEM=="sound", ACTION=="add", KERNEL=="controlC0", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="rotate-audio.service"
